            "url": "https://generesolve.io/fhir/StructureDefinition/etiology-classification",
            "valueString": "single_gene — The patient's presentation of macrocephaly, encephalopathic crisis with dystonia, cerebral atrophy, subdural hemorrhage, and glutaric aciduria is characteristic of Glutaric Aciduria Type 1 (GA-1), which is caused by a deficiency in the glutaryl-CoA dehydrogenase enzyme.. GA-1 is an autosomal recessive disorder caused by mutations in the SLC25A13 gene, leading to a loss of function of the encoded protein. This fits the definition of a single gene disorder with a loss-of-function mechanism"
