    {
      "fullUrl": "urn:uuid:efe539fd-56ea-4951-a208-a463f01d5883",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "ServiceRequest",
        "id": "svcreq-0",
        "status": "draft",
        "intent": "proposal",
        "priority": "urgent",
        "code": {
          "coding": [
            {
              "display": "Enzyme activity assay for Glutaryl-CoA dehydrogenase (GCDH) in fibroblasts or leukocytes"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Enzyme activity assay for Glutaryl-CoA dehydrogenase (GCDH) in fibroblasts or leukocytes"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "urn:uuid:f3572ce8-2ac8-4b93-9894-5db099df7fad"
        },
        "reasonCode": [
          {
            "text": "The patient presents with clinical features (macrocephaly, dystonia, cerebral atrophy, subdural hemorrhage, glutaric aciduria) and a likely pathogenic variant in the GCDH gene, strongly suggesting Glutaric Aciduria Type 1 (GA-1), caused by GCDH deficiency. This test directly measures the function of the enzyme encoded by the top candidate gene."
          }
        ],
        "note": [
          {
            "text": "Power: decisive. A positive result would establish: GCDH deficiency, confirming Glutaric Aciduria Type 1 (GA-1). A negative result would rule out: Functional GCDH enzyme activity, ruling out GA-1 as the primary cause despite the variant; would necessitate re-evaluation of other candidate genes/diseases.."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "urn:uuid:71358b75-2f21-4f2b-987b-e3b30bd6648b",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "ServiceRequest",
        "id": "svcreq-1",
        "status": "draft",
        "intent": "proposal",
        "priority": "routine",
        "code": {
          "coding": [
            {
              "display": "Measurement of plasma or urine acylcarnitine profile"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Measurement of plasma or urine acylcarnitine profile"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "urn:uuid:f3572ce8-2ac8-4b93-9894-5db099df7fad"
        },
        "reasonCode": [
          {
            "text": "The patient has glutaric aciduria and a likely pathogenic variant in GCDH. An acylcarnitine profile can show characteristic elevations (e.g., C5-DC, C6-DC) consistent with GA-1 or other related disorders like Multiple Acyl-CoA Dehydrogenation Deficiency (MAD). While biochemical tests were suggested generally, this specific profile helps differentiate between GA-1 and other potential causes given the overlapping symptoms and candidate genes."
          }
        ],
        "note": [
          {
            "text": "Power: supportive. A positive result would establish: Characteristic acylcarnitine pattern consistent with GA-1 (e.g., elevated C5 dicarboxylic acid), supporting GCDH deficiency.. A negative result would rule out: Acylcarnitine pattern inconsistent with GA-1 or suggestive of another disorder (e.g., MAD), potentially ruling out GA-1 or pointing towards a different diagnosis.."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "urn:uuid:4f13cc77-ebc1-4fbb-8872-87b2dbaeea9e",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "ServiceRequest",
        "id": "svcreq-2",
        "status": "draft",
        "intent": "proposal",
        "priority": "routine",
        "code": {
          "coding": [
            {
              "display": "Genetic testing for SLC25A13 variants"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Genetic testing for SLC25A13 variants"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "urn:uuid:f3572ce8-2ac8-4b93-9894-5db099df7fad"
        },
        "reasonCode": [
          {
            "text": "The Etiology Verdict states that GA-1 is an autosomal recessive disorder caused by mutations in SLC25A13. However, the Ranked Candidate Genes list only includes GCDH. The phenotype strongly suggests GA-1. It is crucial to rule out SLC25A13 mutations if GCDH testing is negative or inconclusive."
          }
        ],
        "note": [
          {
            "text": "Power: exclusionary. A positive result would establish: Presence of two pathogenic variants in SLC25A13, confirming Glutaric Aciduria Type 1 (GA-1) due to SLC25A13 deficiency.. A negative result would rule out: Absence of two pathogenic variants in SLC25A13, making SLC25A13 deficiency unlikely as the cause of GA-1.."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
